### 纠正错误
1. The chinese → Chinese（专有名词首字母大写）；is historical 表达不当，historical 表示 “有关历史的”，描述历史悠久用 has a long history
2. a healthy drinks → a healthy drink；a integral → an integral（integral 元音开头）
3. Diffrent → Different；side 用词错误，应为 regions（地区）；varieties of tea 正确，也可用 various types of tea
4. rea tea → black tea（红茶固定表达）；WuLong tea → oolong tea
5. chat easily 用词不准，easily 是 “容易地”，闲谈用 casually；families 改为 relatives（亲友：relatives and friends）
6. passed through all over the world 搭配错误，传播用 spread；tea skills 茶艺改为 tea art；feel the unique beauty 改为 experience the unique charm（charm 更贴合文化魅力）


### 美化原句
Chinese tea culture has a long history. Chinese people love drinking tea. Tea is not only a healthy drink but also an integral part of traditional culture. Different regions
produce various types of tea, such as green tea, black tea and oolong tea. People often taste tea and chat casually with relatives and friends in their spare time. Nowadays,
tea culture has spread all over the world, and more and more foreigners begin to learn tea art to experience the unique charm of Chinese culture.


### 标准参照句
Chinese tea culture boasts a long history. Chinese people are fond of drinking tea. Tea serves not only as a healthy beverage but also as an integral component of traditional 
culture. Different regions yield diverse categories of tea, including green tea, black tea and oolong tea. In their leisure time, people often savour tea and chat casually with
relatives and friends. At present, tea culture has spread across the globe. An increasing number of foreigners are learning tea art to appreciate the distinctive charm of 
Chinese culture.

